{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\n\nFound while proving the root cause of bug 4bf4 (jscpd live-clone fixture below the token\nfloor). Not a blocker for 4bf4 — filed so the observation is not lost.\n\n`rebar.metrics.analyzers._jscpd.run_jscpd` reads `statistics.total.{clones,percentage}` and\nreturns them verbatim. When **no file in the scanned tree clears jscpd's `--min-tokens`\nfloor (default 50)**, jscpd 5.0.14 returns:\n\n    {\"clones\": 0, \"percentage\": 0.0, \"sources\": 0, \"lines\": 0, \"tokens\": 0}\n\nThat is byte-identical in the two fields rebar reads to a tree that genuinely has no\nduplication. So `rebar metrics` would report \"0% duplication\" for a tree jscpd never actually\nexamined.\n\n## Why it may matter\n\nThe project already holds the invariant that jscpd failing to answer must surface as\n`Unavailable` rather than zero — see\n`tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py::test_failed_jscpd_is_unavailable_not_zero`,\nand 4bf4's own AC3: \"a metric that reads 0 when it means 'I cannot tell' is worse than\n`unavailable`\". `sources == 0` is arguably that same case, and is currently reported as a\nconfident zero.\n\n## Why it was NOT fixed under 4bf4\n\nIt needs a judgment call rather than a bugfix, and 4bf4's proven root cause was solely the\ntest fixture. Options:\n\n1. **Treat `sources == 0` as unavailable.** Honest, matches the existing invariant. But it\n   turns a legitimately-tiny or empty tree from \"0% duplication\" into \"unavailable\", which\n   some callers may find noisier. Note `statistics.total.sources` is absent from the minimal\n   report shape used by `tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup.py::test_parse_statistics_total`,\n   so the check must be `.get(\"sources\")` and fire only on an explicit `0`.\n2. **Leave as-is.** On any real repository at least one file clears a 50-token floor, so\n   `sources > 0` in practice and the ambiguity never materializes.\n3. **Surface `sources` alongside the totals** so callers can decide, without changing the\n   current availability semantics.\n\nNo option is obviously correct without a product view on what the duplication metric should\nsay about a tree too small to measure. Recommend option 1 or 3 if picked up.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A decision is recorded on which of the three options applies.\n- [x] If option 1 or 3: duplication over a tree where no source clears the token floor is\n      distinguishable from genuine zero duplication, with a regression test.\n- [x] `tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup.py::test_parse_statistics_total` continues to pass\n      unmodified (its report fixture omits `sources`).\n\n## Duplicate resolution evidence\n\nThis ticket duplicates dental-catty-dorado. That closed ticket selected option 1: an explicit statistics.total.sources == 0 result is Unavailable, while a report that omits sources preserves the existing genuine-zero behavior. Merged commit aeb4e036a6ba431e85837acec9d47188f4df0038 contains the exact guard and held-out regression test. Its recorded experiments distinguish an unmeasured tree (sources: 0) from a measured no-duplication tree (sources: 2, clones: 0, percentage: 0.0), and the mutation check reintroduced the ambiguous confident-zero result. Current origin/main contains that commit and behavior.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786386374210179001,"uuid":"86905eef-2ce1-469f-9578-a416a2fc2eed"}